Subject: [PATCH] procd: run service instances as transient systemd units

With --systemd=units, each capable instance is started as a transient
openwrt-SERVICE@INSTANCE.service in openwrt-SERVICE.slice. systemd
executes, restarts (Restart=, RestartSec=, start limits derived from the
procd respawn settings), logs to the journal, contains and stops the
processes. procd keeps the ubus service/system/hotplug API, triggers,
validation, data and configuration comparison. Unit state arrives as
D-Bus signals on systemd's private socket and is applied from uloop.

Instances using vrf, trace, OCI bundles, passed descriptors or a jail
console keep the existing fork and scope path.

udev owns uevents and device nodes in this mode. Device events with
OpenWrt handlers are forwarded by openwrt-udev-forward to a root-only
procd.udev ubus object and run through /etc/hotplug-systemd.json; procd
still reads the synthetic button events, which udev cannot see. Once per
boot procd requests "add" for every device through udevadm, as udevtrigger
did. systemd owns the hardware watchdog; "system watchdog" reports it
read-only.

